3.2 Hand gesture recognition
A hand gesture recognition (HGR) system is classified into several basic steps involving acquisition of the image, detection and segmentation of the hand, hand tracking and finally the classification of gestures [34]. However, since our recognition process can work at the same rate as acquisition of the image, tracking is not required. Thus, our HGR system consists of image acquisition, segmentation and identification, extraction of features, and gesture recognition. Section 3.2.1 briefly describes the process of hand detection and gesture image segmentation, and Sections 3.2.2 and 3.2.3 describe the process of feature extraction and the details of the classification of gesture functions.

